---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { heroDefinition } from '../content/snippets';
---

<Site
  title="EvalKit — author agent evals as code"
  description="A local-first kit for writing agent evals as code. Version definitions with your team, reuse fixtures and predicate judges, compare model settings, and inspect saved results."
  active="home"
>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h1 id="hero-title">Write evals <em>as code</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">Define an agent task in TypeScript, run it locally, and inspect the evidence it leaves behind. Your definitions belong in Git; your results stay on disk.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="/docs/">Run your first eval <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a class="button button-quiet" href="https://github.com/leostera/evalkit">View source <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-code">
      <div class="code-card">
        <div class="code-header"><span>examples/starter/evals/greeting.eval.ts</span><span class="code-header-right">TypeScript</span></div>
        <pre><code>{heroDefinition}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <a class="hero-code-source" href="https://github.com/leostera/evalkit/blob/main/examples/starter/evals/greeting.eval.ts">Open the runnable source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap workflow" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="workflow-title">From definition to evidence.</h2>
      <p>Write the test alongside your app, then inspect what the agent actually did. No hosted account is required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="workflow-list">
      <article class="workflow-item">
        <h3>Define the task</h3>
        <div><p>Describe the transcript, trial policy, and success criteria in TypeScript. Review changes to the eval like any other code.</p><a href="/docs/manual/scoring-and-evals/">Evals and scoring <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="workflow-item">
        <h3>Keep inputs separate</h3>
        <div><p>Reuse fixtures across trials. Give the agent only candidate-visible files; keep reference answers in the evaluator workspace.</p><a href="/docs/manual/fixtures/">Fixtures and visibility <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="workflow-item">
        <h3>Change a parameter</h3>
        <div><p>Run the same eval across selected matrix settings. Your agent adapter decides how each parameter changes its behavior.</p><a href="/docs/manual/cli-and-matrices/">Matrices and runs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap output-section" aria-labelledby="output-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="output-title">The run is yours to inspect.</h2>
      <p>EvalKit writes a local report, not a score hidden behind a service. Read the event stream, check why a rule passed, or open the files the agent produced.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/manual/results/">Understand reports <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="report" aria-label="Example report file structure">
      <div class="report-heading">_evalkit-results/&lt;run-id&gt;/</div>
      <div class="report-row"><code>summary.json</code><span>Run-level counts and status</span></div>
      <div class="report-heading report-nested">trials/&lt;trial-id&gt;/</div>
      <div class="report-row report-nested"><code>trajectory.jsonl</code><span>Recorded events in order</span></div>
      <div class="report-row report-nested"><code>scoring.json</code><span>Values, explanations, evidence</span></div>
      <div class="report-row report-nested"><code>artifacts/candidate/</code><span>Files from the agent workspace</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
    <div class="wrap cta-content">
      <div><h2 id="cta-title">Start with a working eval.</h2><p>The scaffold runs without a model key. Bring your own agent when you're ready.</p></div>
      <a class="button button-dark" href="/docs/">Read the getting-started guide <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
